IMPORT prelude

-- Merchant Shipping (Wreck Removal) Act 2017 (Singapore) -- what a "wreck" is and when the Act applies (ss 2, 3, 20(1)), the duty to
-- report a wreck and the offence of not doing so (s 4), when the Director may remove a wreck (ss 5, 7, 8), the registered owner's
-- liability for the Director's costs and its exceptions (s 10, with Article 10(1) of the Convention), the time bar (s 13), compulsory
-- wreck removal insurance for ships of 300 gross tonnage and above (ss 14, 15, 20(2) and the Second Schedule), certificates (s 16),
-- the Director's direct claim against the insurer (s 17), the maximum fines (ss 4(7), 15(4), (5), 23(5)) and composition (s 28).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/MSWRA2017.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the retrieval
-- record calls it the current version as at 1 October 2026. The Legislative History lists only the original Act 25 of 2017
-- (commencement 8 September 2017); no later amendment is annotated in the body.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0108 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. A business meets this Act when it owns, operates or insures a ship of 300 gross tonnage or more that calls at a
-- Singapore port, or flies the Singapore flag, and when one of its ships sinks, strands or loses cargo at sea. Not encoded: the
-- Director's duties to locate and mark (s 6, Arts 7, 8) and the Article 6 hazard criteria (s 9) beyond a yes/no "determined to be a
-- hazard"; sale of the wreck (s 8(3)); limitation of liability, which s 12 hands to Part 8 of the Merchant Shipping Act 1995 (not
-- read); detention (s 15(6), (7)); admiralty jurisdiction and recourse (ss 18, 19); arrest, boarding, search and the corporate
-- officer provisions (ss 21 to 25) beyond the s 23(5) penalty; immunity, extra-territoriality, exemption and regulations
-- (ss 26, 27, 29 to 31); and the rest of the Convention text in the First Schedule. No regulations were retrieved, so which offences
-- are compoundable, the fees and the evidence of insurance required are unknown.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Merchant Shipping (Wreck Removal) Act 2017 -- wrecks`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` a b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `2, 3 and 20(1) -- what a wreck is, and when the Act applies`

-- s 2: "wreck", following upon a maritime casualty, means "(a) a sunken or stranded ship; (b) any part of a sunken or stranded ship,
-- including any object that is or has been on board such a ship; (c) any object that is lost at sea from a ship and that is
-- stranded, sunken or adrift at sea; or (d) a ship that is about, or may reasonably be expected, to sink or to strand, where
-- effective measures to assist the ship or any property in danger are not already being taken."
-- "maritime casualty" means "a collision of ships, stranding or other incident of navigation, or other occurrence on board a ship or
-- external to it, resulting in material damage or imminent threat of material damage to a ship or its cargo".
DECLARE Object IS ONE OF
    `a sunken ship`
    `a stranded ship`
    `a container lost overboard and adrift`
    `a ship expected to sink`
    `a damaged ship still afloat and not expected to sink`

GIVEN `the object` IS AN Object,
      `follows a maritime casualty` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `effective assistance is already being given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the object is a wreck` IF
    `follows a maritime casualty` AND
    (CONSIDER `the object`
     WHEN `a ship expected to sink` THEN NOT `effective assistance is already being given`
     WHEN `a damaged ship still afloat and not expected to sink` THEN FALSE
     OTHERWISE TRUE)

-- s 3: "Nothing in this Act applies in relation to any wreck following upon a maritime casualty occurring before 8 September 2017."
-- s 20(1): subject to (3), nothing in the Act applies to "(a) any warship; or (b) any ship for the time being used by the government
-- of any State otherwise than for commercial purposes". (s 20(3), which brings such a ship under Part 4 when its State so notifies
-- under Article 4(3), is not modelled.) Dates are written as YYYYMMDD numbers.
GIVEN `date of the casualty` IS A NUMBER, `is a warship or non-commercial government ship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies to the wreck` IF
    `date of the casualty` AT LEAST 20170908 AND (NOT `is a warship or non-commercial government ship`)

§§ `4 -- reporting a wreck`

-- s 2: "Convention area" means "the exclusive economic zone of a State Party" (or, where none is established, an area "beyond and
-- adjacent to the territorial sea" up to 200 nautical miles); "Singapore's Convention area" means "the exclusive economic zone of
-- Singapore".
-- s 4(1): where "a Singapore ship is involved in a maritime casualty resulting in a wreck in a Convention area other than Singapore's
-- Convention area, the master or the operator of that ship must report the wreck to the government of the affected State without
-- delay". (2): a wreck "in Singapore's Convention area" -- report "to the Director without delay".
-- The Act defines no duty for a wreck outside every Convention area, nor (on the face of these definitions) for one in a
-- territorial sea or port, which is not exclusive economic zone. That reading of "exclusive economic zone" is an INFERENCE.
DECLARE Location IS ONE OF
    `in Singapore's Convention area`
    `in another State Party's Convention area`
    `in Singapore's territorial sea or port`
    `outside any Convention area`

DECLARE Recipient IS ONE OF
    `the Director`
    `the government of the affected State`
    `no one under section 4`

GIVEN `is a Singapore ship` IS A BOOLEAN, `where the wreck is` IS A Location
GIVETH A Recipient
`the wreck must be reported to` MEANS
    IF NOT `is a Singapore ship` THEN `no one under section 4`
    ELSE CONSIDER `where the wreck is`
         WHEN `in Singapore's Convention area` THEN `the Director`
         WHEN `in another State Party's Convention area` THEN `the government of the affected State`
         OTHERWISE `no one under section 4`

-- s 4(3): the report must contain the registered owner's name and principal place of business and, so far as known, the location,
-- type, size and construction, damage and condition, cargo (especially hazardous and noxious substances) and oil on board.
-- (4): "If any of the persons mentioned in subsection (1) or (2) makes a report under that subsection, the other person mentioned in
-- that subsection is not required to make the report."
-- (5): "If a report required to be made ... is not made, the master and the operator of the ship shall each be guilty of an offence."
-- (6): "If the report made ... does not comply with subsection (3), the master or the operator of the ship who made the report shall
-- be guilty of an offence." (7): fine not exceeding $10,000.
DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `the master`
    `the operator`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Role,
      `a report was required` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the master reported` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the operator reported` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the report made was complete` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits an offence under section 4` IF
    `a report was required` AND
    (    ((NOT `the master reported`) AND (NOT `the operator reported`))
     OR  ((NOT `the report made was complete`) AND
          (CONSIDER `the person`
           WHEN `the master` THEN `the master reported`
           WHEN `the operator` THEN `the operator reported`)))

§§ `5, 7 and 8 -- when the Director may remove the wreck`

-- s 5: Part 3 "applies where a ship is involved in a maritime casualty resulting in a wreck in Singapore's Convention area".
-- s 7(1), (2): once the Director determines a wreck to be a hazard, the Director gives the registered owner written notice to remove
-- it, with "a reasonable deadline", and states that the Director "may remove the wreck at the registered owner's expense".
-- s 8(1): "The Director may remove a wreck which the Director has determined to constitute a hazard -- (a) where the registered owner
-- of the ship does not remove the wreck within the deadline specified in the notice ...; (b) where the registered owner of the ship
-- cannot be contacted; or (c) where the Director has determined that having regard to the nature of the hazard immediate action must
-- be taken to remove the wreck."
GIVEN `in Singapore's Convention area` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `determined to be a hazard` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `deadline passed without removal` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `owner cannot be contacted` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `immediate action needed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director may remove the wreck` IF
        `in Singapore's Convention area`
    AND `determined to be a hazard`
    AND (`deadline passed without removal` OR `owner cannot be contacted` OR `immediate action needed`)

§§ `10 -- liability for the Director's costs`

-- s 10(1), (2): where a ship's maritime casualty results in a wreck in Singapore's Convention area and the Director incurs costs "for
-- locating, marking and removing the wreck under Part 3", "the registered owner of the ship is liable for the Director's costs".
-- (3): not liable "if or to the extent that liability for the costs would conflict with" a convention listed in Article 11(1) (oil
-- pollution, hazardous and noxious substances, nuclear, bunker oil) that is in force in Singapore, an enactment implementing one, or
-- a provision specified by order.
-- (4): not liable "if the registered owner of the ship proves that an exception set out in paragraph 1(a), (b) or (c) of Article 10
-- of the Convention applies". Article 10(1): the casualty "(a) resulted from an act of war, hostilities, civil war, insurrection, or a
-- natural phenomenon of an exceptional, inevitable and irresistible character; (b) was WHOLLY caused by an act or omission done with
-- intent to cause damage by a third party; or (c) was WHOLLY caused by the negligence or other wrongful act of any Government or other
-- authority responsible for the maintenance of lights or other navigational aids".
-- (6): the registered owner is the one "at the time of the maritime casualty". The "to the extent" partial case is not modelled.
DECLARE Cause IS ONE OF
    `a navigational error by the crew`
    `an act of war`
    `an exceptional, inevitable and irresistible natural phenomenon`
    `a third party's sabotage, wholly`
    `a third party's sabotage, partly`
    `an authority's negligent maintenance of navigational lights, wholly`

GIVEN `the cause` IS A Cause
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cause is an Article 10 exception` IF
    CONSIDER `the cause`
    WHEN `a navigational error by the crew` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a third party's sabotage, partly` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `wreck in Singapore's Convention area` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `Director incurred costs under Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `liability conflicts with a listed convention` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the cause of the casualty` IS A Cause,
      `the owner proves the cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the registered owner is liable for the Director's costs` IF
        `wreck in Singapore's Convention area`
    AND `Director incurred costs under Part 3`
    AND (NOT `liability conflicts with a listed convention`)
    AND (NOT (`the owner proves the cause` AND `the cause is an Article 10 exception` `the cause of the casualty`))

§§ `13 -- time bar`

-- s 13: an action to recover costs under s 10 "may not be brought unless the action is commenced on or before the earlier of the
-- following: (a) the end of the period of 3 years after the date on which the notice by the Director is given under section 7;
-- (b) the end of the period of 6 years after the date of the maritime casualty which resulted in the wreck."
-- Dates are YYYYMMDD numbers, so "3 years after" is + 30000 (the same calendar date; 29 February is not handled). Section 13 does
-- not say what happens where no s 7 notice was given (as where the owner could not be contacted, s 8(1)(b)); this encoding then
-- applies the 6-year limb alone -- an INFERENCE.
GIVEN `date of the casualty` IS A NUMBER, `a section 7 notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN, `date of the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day to sue for the costs` MEANS
    IF `a section 7 notice was given`
    THEN `the smaller of` (`date of the notice` PLUS 30000) (`date of the casualty` PLUS 60000)
    ELSE `date of the casualty` PLUS 60000

GIVEN `date of the casualty` IS A NUMBER, `a section 7 notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN, `date of the notice` IS A NUMBER,
      `date the action is commenced` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the action is in time` IF
    `date the action is commenced` AT MOST `the last day to sue for the costs` `date of the casualty` `a section 7 notice was given` `date of the notice`

§§ `14, 15, 20(2) and Second Schedule -- compulsory insurance`

-- s 14(1): Division 2 "applies to a ship, other than an excluded ship, having a gross tonnage of 300 or above".
-- Second Schedule: an excluded ship is one which "(a) is operated under a licence or permit, or is exempted from the requirement of a
-- licence or permit under" the MPA (Harbour Craft) or (Pleasure Craft) Regulations; "(b) is insured under such policy of insurance
-- covering the registered owner's liability under this Act as required by the Port Master under those Regulations; and (c)
-- navigates exclusively in areas within the limits of the port".
-- s 15(1): "A Singapore ship may not enter or leave a port in Singapore, or a port in a country other than Singapore, unless -- (a)
-- the ship is covered by wreck removal insurance; (b) the Director has certified that the ship is covered by wreck removal insurance;
-- and (c) a copy of the Director's certificate is carried on board the ship."
-- (2): "A foreign ship may not enter or leave a port in Singapore unless -- (a) the ship is covered by wreck removal insurance; and
-- (b) there is carried on board the ship written evidence of paragraph (a)."
-- s 20(2): s 15 "does not apply to a ship that is owned by a State Party if there is carried on board the ship a certificate issued by
-- the State Party" that it owns the ship and that s 10 liability will be met up to the s 12 limit.
-- s 15(4): in contravention, "the master and the operator of the ship shall each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on
-- conviction to a fine not exceeding $20,000".
DECLARE Ship HAS
    `is a Singapore ship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gross tonnage` IS A NUMBER
    `is a licensed or exempted harbour or pleasure craft` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is insured as the Port Master requires` IS A BOOLEAN
    `navigates only within port limits` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is covered by wreck removal insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has the Director's certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `carries a copy of the Director's certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `carries written evidence of insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is State Party owned and carries its State's certificate` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the ship` IS A Ship
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ship is an excluded ship` IF
        `the ship`'s `is a licensed or exempted harbour or pleasure craft`
    AND `the ship`'s `is insured as the Port Master requires`
    AND `the ship`'s `navigates only within port limits`

GIVEN `the ship` IS A Ship
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Division 2 applies to the ship` IF
    `the ship`'s `gross tonnage` AT LEAST 300 AND (NOT `the ship is an excluded ship` `the ship`)

GIVEN `the ship` IS A Ship, `the port is in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 15 bars the ship from entering or leaving the port` IF
        `Division 2 applies to the ship` `the ship`
    AND (NOT `the ship`'s `is State Party owned and carries its State's certificate`)
    AND (IF `the ship`'s `is a Singapore ship`
         THEN NOT (`the ship`'s `is covered by wreck removal insurance`
                   AND `the ship`'s `has the Director's certificate`
                   AND `the ship`'s `carries a copy of the Director's certificate`)
         ELSE `the port is in Singapore`
              AND (NOT (`the ship`'s `is covered by wreck removal insurance` AND `the ship`'s `carries written evidence of insurance`)))

§§ `16 -- certificates`

-- s 16(1), (2): the registered owner of a Singapore ship may apply, and "the Director must issue the certificate ... if the Director
-- is satisfied that the ship is covered by wreck removal insurance". (3): the Director "may refuse to issue the certificate if the
-- Director has any doubt as to" whether the insurer's obligations will be met or the insurance will satisfy Article 12 "in all
-- circumstances".
-- (4), (5): the registered owner of a foreign ship "registered in any country that is not a State Party" may also apply, and the
-- Director "may" issue it if satisfied of cover, and may refuse on a (3) ground "without prejudice to any other ground".
-- No application under s 16 is provided for a foreign ship registered in a State Party (an observation on the text: Article 12(2)
-- has its own State certify it).
DECLARE Outcome IS ONE OF
    `the Director must issue`
    `the Director may issue or refuse`
    `the Director may refuse`
    `no certificate, as cover is not shown`
    `no application lies under section 16`

GIVEN `is a Singapore ship` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `registered in a State Party` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `cover is shown` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Director has a doubt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Outcome
`the certificate application outcome` MEANS
    IF (NOT `is a Singapore ship`) AND `registered in a State Party` THEN `no application lies under section 16`
    ELSE IF NOT `cover is shown` THEN `no certificate, as cover is not shown`
         ELSE IF NOT `is a Singapore ship` THEN `the Director may issue or refuse`
              ELSE IF `the Director has a doubt` THEN `the Director may refuse`
                   ELSE `the Director must issue`

§§ `17 -- the Director's claim against the insurer`

-- s 17(1), (2): where the ship was "at the time of the maritime casualty" covered by wreck removal insurance and the registered owner
-- is liable under s 10, "the Director may recover the costs from the person providing the wreck removal insurance".
-- (3): "It is a defence for the insurer ... to prove that the maritime casualty was caused by the wilful misconduct of the registered
-- owner of the ship." (4): the insurer "may also rely on any defences available to the registered owner". (5): the insurer may limit
-- liability as the owner may, "whether or not the maritime casualty resulted from any act or omission of the registered owner".
GIVEN `covered at the time of the casualty` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the owner is liable under section 10` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `insurer proves the owner's wilful misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director may recover from the insurer` IF
        `covered at the time of the casualty`
    AND `the owner is liable under section 10`
    AND (NOT `insurer proves the owner's wilful misconduct`)

§§ `4(7), 15(4), (5), 23(5) and 28 -- penalties and composition`

-- s 4(7): $10,000 for a reporting offence. s 15(4): $20,000 each for master and operator for entering or leaving without cover.
-- s 15(5): $20,000 for a master who fails to carry or produce the certificate or evidence. s 23(5): obstructing an authorised officer,
-- misstating or refusing information -- "a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to
-- both".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `failing to report a wreck`
    `making an incomplete report`
    `entering or leaving a port without cover`
    `failing to carry or produce the certificate`
    `obstructing an authorised officer`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `failing to report a wreck` THEN 10000
    WHEN `making an incomplete report` THEN 10000
    OTHERWISE 20000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `obstructing an authorised officer` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 0

-- s 28(1): the Director may compound an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" by collecting "a sum not exceeding the lower of
-- the following: (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $1,000." Which offences are
-- prescribed is for regulations (s 31(2)(c)), none retrieved.
GIVEN `maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that may be collected to compound` MEANS
    `the smaller of` (`maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2) 1000
